# Hot code upgrade

```elixir
Mix.install([{:elixir_harness, path: "."}])
```

Recompile a tool module and reload it into the running VM —
`:code.purge/1` + `:code.load_binary/3`, the same per-module mechanism
`mix release` upgrades use. The session never drops.

```elixir
{:ok, s} = ElixirHarness.Session.start_link()
ElixirHarness.Session.append(s, "user", "greet me")
:ok = ElixirHarness.Showcase.Upgrade.deploy(ElixirHarness.UpgradeDemo.Greeter, 1)
ElixirHarness.UpgradeDemo.Greeter.greet("agent")
:ok = ElixirHarness.Showcase.Upgrade.deploy(ElixirHarness.UpgradeDemo.Greeter, 2)
ElixirHarness.UpgradeDemo.Greeter.greet("agent")
ElixirHarness.Session.history(s)
```

Or the narrated version: `mix showcase upgrade`.

Production path: the same calls happen per-module inside a proper
`mix release` + `release_handler` upgrade. The demo shows the mechanism;
releases add the orchestration (appup, ordering, rollback).
